// m21 — "The Verdict" / "Status: Open" (neural-net-history, ch15-s08/s09; ch15-s10 is silent). Window
// 2039.417–2139.5417 (100.125 s; CLOCK RE-FIT 2026-10-12: the film now ends at 2139.5417, every event +18.25 s), fadeIn 0, fadeOut 0, tail 10: the window runs to the film's end; the last chord
// rings out under the fade to black and the Turing card and has decayed by about 2121; the rest of the body is silent (room tone covers it).
// Rubato at 60 BPM: setcps(1), one cycle = one second; events written at their ABSOLUTE film second through
// A(t) = t − 2039.417. Intensity 0.5, peak 0.7 (the bloom, in the clear).
//
//  2039.52 THE FAST-FORWARD (on the cut, from silence after m20's beat of silence): tape lurch (a string chord
//        spinning up an octave + hiss), then clean: five 0.75-s flashes, each a short forward swell in its era's
//        colour: 2040.42 valve organ (the knob, A), 2041.17 bowed glass + cello (snow, Bm), 2041.92 oscillator
//        (the fans, F#m), 2042.67 harp (the Go stone, Em), 2043.42 celesta over a soft low D (the wick in the box):
//        the fifth lands on D, alone for 0.8 s before L1527 (2044.22).
//  2044.22–2054.76 THE VERDICT: a hush; one dry grey pluck each for RULES (2045.76) and KNOWLEDGE (2047.15), the
//        same note, no harmony. "Learning" 2049.35: M1's rising fourth (celesta A->D) as the LEARNING lantern
//        lights, D major in the high strings. "accomplices": one high harp pluck per accomplice, rising D F# A D
//        (M3's forward pass): data 2051.18, fire 2051.9, a messenger 2052.77, people 2053.93.
//  2055.46–2059.27 THE NETWORK "Never one person. The board was a network all along.": M3's forward wave crosses
//        the lantern network, one era instrument per column every 0.44 s (celesta 2055.46, valve organ 2055.9,
//        cello 2056.34, piano 2056.78, oscillator pulse 2057.22, harp 2057.66, pizz 2058.09 on "network"), each
//        rippling D F# A D and staying on as a layer. REVIEW NOTE (MAJOR): the layers stay at about a third of
//        their velocity, everything between D3 and D5 behind lpf 900, music at least 10 dB under the voice for
//        the whole line; nothing blooms until the line has ended.
//  2059.35 THE BLOOM in the gap (2059.27–2061.51): the trained forward pass D3 F#3 A3 D4 lands on the third, F#
//        (2059.91): full D major (strings, horns, harp roll, contrabass, one timpani stroke, celesta F#), HELD to
//        2061.05 and thin by 2061.35, leaving solo celesta: the film's fullest moment and the loudest of the score.
//  2061.51–2068.36 THE BAR CHART IN WAX, one celesta note per candle: "forty" 2062.8 (low, long), "two" 2064.47
//        (short), "a day" 2066.49 (the shortest tick), "still burn" 2067.67 (a held D: still lit).
//  2070.31 "dark": everything drops to ONE held note, E (the lit box's question tone: piano E6, held in strings
//        and glass) through "how, exactly, it reaches its answers", "That file stays open" and the hold.
//  2082.71/2083.2 THE LAST SLIP (on the cut, decaying under L1517 from 2083.51): solo celesta, the slip motif with m12's pitches (written a3 -> d4), slowed; the
//        D held in the high strings while a soft A-E fifth slides in beneath (2085.25); the quote (2088.06–2094.34)
//        over the held D only; all of it gone by 2094.1.
//  2094.1–2097.85 SILENCE: the stamp (2094.75) and the lamp click (2097.25).
//  2098.26–2104.4 M4's walk, solo cello, very soft, below D3: A1 D2 E2 F2 G2 ("rim") F2 E2 C2 D2.
//  2104.80 the struck match in near silence.
//  2105.46/2106.24 THE LAST GESTURE: as the new candle catches, celesta M1 rises once more, A->D, held;
//  2107.8 at the cut to black the strings and contrabass slide in beneath it to A-E: Asus4, the held D the
//        suspension; a solo cello takes the held D at D3 in the middle of the chord (v3). Last onset 2107.8
//        (inside ch15-s10's 1.6-s fade to black, centred on 2108.04).
//        It does NOT resolve; it rings out under the Turing card.
//  v3 (2026-10-11): the question tone E6 struck once more after "That file stays open" (2077.87, in the clear) and the
//        dark lantern's held E carried to the cut (2082.71); the last chord's D doubled by cello in the middle.
//  v4 (critic round 1): the bloom uses the whole gap, held at full D major to 2061.05 and about 4 dB louder
//        (aim -13 LUFS M in the render, the score's peak); the last chord about 1.5 dB up; the slip moved onto
//        the cut (A 2082.71, D 2083.2, the celesta sustaining only 1 s) so its D is already decaying when L1517
//        starts, the strings holding the D; the dark lantern's E released faster (1.5 s) off the cut.
//  v5 (2026-10-12, voice-band pass): L1517 was re-narrated 0.09 s shorter, so from the quote on every event is 0.09 s
//        earlier (stamp 2094.75, lamp 2097.25, the walk from 2098.26, 'rim' 2101.16, match 2104.80, the candle 2106.24); the
//        last chord stays at 2107.8, inside ch15-s10's fade to black. Measured per line in the 250-2k and 1-4k voice bands,
//        v4 kept only 3.6 dB clear under 'Learning, with its accomplices' (the D-major string halo at D5-A5 and the long
//        celesta ring), 1.7 dB in L1514's consonant band (the high era layers), 2.4 dB under L1517 (the slip's ringing D)
//        and 4.5 under 'One lantern is still dark' (the held E5): the halo is now a halo (.02, lpf 1800), the celesta Ds
//        struck and let go, the high network layers a further -6 dB (the bloom itself untouched: still the score's
//        loudest moment, in the clear), the held E -3.7 dB under the lines and re-bowed at full level in the clear after
//        'That file stays open'. Every line now 7.6-21 dB clear in both bands.
setcps(1)
const S = 2039.417
const A = (t) => +(t - S).toFixed(3)
const N = 101       // seconds covered by each compiled sequence (the window is 100.125 s; onsets end at 2107.8)
const G = 2.0       // master trim (postgain): old-clock render 5 measured -22.0 LUFS at 2.0 (bloom -14.7 M);
                    // new-clock v1 -22.4, but the beds under L1527/L1515/L1517 sat only 1-7 dB under the voice:
                    // v2 lowers every layer under a line (the hush, Learning, the slip, the walk) and keeps the gaps
const W3 = 1 / 3    // the network's era layers under L1514: about a third of their velocity (review, MAJOR)
const WH = .5       // v5: the HIGH era layers (celesta, piano, harp, top strings) a further -6 dB: L1514's 1-4 kHz
                    // band (the consonants of the thesis line) measured only 1.7 dB clear of them in v4

// ---- shared helper: events in cue-local SECONDS (setcps(1): one cycle = one second = one beat at 60 BPM) ----
// [start, dur, notes, velocity, {per-event params}] compiled into one mini-notation sequence per lane
// (overlapping events go to new lanes), so every onset sits exactly where the clock needs it.
function line(evs, defs) {
  defs = defs || {}
  const sorted = [...evs].sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0])
  const lanes = []
  for (const e of sorted) {
    let lane = lanes.find((l) => l.end <= e[0] + 1e-6)
    if (!lane) { lane = { end: 0, evs: [] }; lanes.push(lane) }
    lane.evs.push(e)
    lane.end = e[0] + e[1]
  }
  const keys = Object.keys(defs)
  const seq = (lane, val) => {
    let pos = 0
    const out = []
    for (const e of lane.evs) {
      if (e[0] - pos > 1e-6) out.push('~@' + (e[0] - pos).toFixed(4))
      out.push(val(e) + '@' + e[1].toFixed(4))
      pos = e[0] + e[1]
    }
    if (N - pos > 1e-6) out.push('~@' + (N - pos).toFixed(4))
    return mini('[' + out.join(' ') + ']')
  }
  return stack(...lanes.map((lane) => {
    let p = note(seq(lane, (e) => e[2])).velocity(seq(lane, (e) => e[3]))
    for (const k of keys) p = p[k](seq(lane, (e) => (e[4] && e[4][k] != null ? e[4][k] : defs[k])))
    return p.slow(N).postgain(G)
  }))
}

// ---- THE FAST-FORWARD ----
// tape lurch: a low string chord that spins up an octave as the tape catches, with a breath of hiss
$: line([[A(2039.52), .8, '[d2,a2,d3]', .2]], { attack: .3, release: .25 })
  .s('gm_string_ensemble_1').penv(12).pattack(.7).lpf(1600).room(.3).rsize(2).orbit(1)
$: line([[A(2039.52), .85, 'd4', .5]], { attack: .45, release: .2 })
  .s('pink').hpf(1200).lpf(6000).gain(.05).orbit(1)
// the forward swells (strings): A, Bm, F#m, Em, then a soft D that stays for the hush
$: line([
  [A(2040.42), .5, '[a2,e3,a3,c#4]', .15], [A(2041.17), .5, '[b2,f#3,b3,d4]', .15], [A(2041.92), .5, '[f#2,c#3,f#3,a3]', .15],
  [A(2042.67), .5, '[e2,b2,e3,g3]', .15],
  [A(2043.42), 5.6, '[d2,a2,d3]', .045, { attack: .5, release: 1.6, lpf: 800 }],
], { attack: .3, release: .35, lpf: 2200 })
  .s('gm_string_ensemble_1').room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(2)
// each era's colour on its flash
$: line([[A(2040.42), .5, '[a3,e4]', .24]], { attack: .2, release: .3 }).s('gm_drawbar_organ').lpf(1500).room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(2)
$: line([[A(2041.17), .5, '[f#4,b4]', .16]], { attack: .25, release: .4 }).s('gm_pad_bowed').room(.5).rsize(3).orbit(2)
$: line([[A(2041.17), .5, 'b2', .22]], { attack: .2, release: .4 }).s('gm_cello').lpf(1200).room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(2)
$: line([[A(2041.92), .5, '[f#2,c#3,f#3]', .5]], { attack: .2, release: .3 }).s('sawtooth').lpf(1300).gain(.12).room(.3).rsize(3).orbit(2)
$: line([[A(2042.67), .5, '[e3,b3,e4,g4]', .2]], { release: 1 }).s('gm_orchestral_harp').room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(2)

// ---- THE VERDICT: grey plucks (dry, same note), then LEARNING and its accomplices ----
$: line([[A(2045.76), .2, 'e2', .28], [A(2047.15), .2, 'e2', .28]], { release: .15 })
  .s('gm_pizzicato_strings').lpf(650).room(.08).rsize(1).orbit(3)
// one high harp pluck per accomplice (above the voice): D F# A D, M3's forward pass, the last left ringing
$: line([
  [A(2051.18), .6, 'd5', .075], [A(2051.9), .6, 'f#5', .075], [A(2052.77), .6, 'a5', .075], [A(2053.93), 1.2, 'd6', .085, { release: 2 }],
], { release: 1.2 })
  .s('gm_orchestral_harp').pan(.5).room(.55).rsize(4).orbit(3)

// SOLO CELESTA (sounds an octave above the written note): the wick (the fifth flash), "Learning", the wave's
// first column (a third) and its ticking ostinato (a third), the trained pass's F#, the bar chart in wax,
// the last slip, the last gesture.
const osc = []
for (let t = A(2056.02); t < A(2059.2); t += .25) osc.push([t, .25, Math.round((t - A(2056.02)) / .25) % 2 ? 'd5' : 'a4', .14 * W3 * WH])
$: line([
  [A(2043.42), .8, '[d4,a4]', .13, { release: 1.2 }],   // v5: decayed before 'Who'
  [A(2048.87), .48, 'a3', .17], [A(2049.35), 1.6, 'd4', .18, { release: 2.2 }],   // v5: -2 dB, shorter ring under 'accomplices'
  [A(2055.46), .11, 'd4', .26 * W3 * WH], [A(2055.57), .11, 'f#4', .26 * W3 * WH], [A(2055.68), .11, 'a4', .26 * W3 * WH], [A(2055.79), .2, 'd5', .26 * W3 * WH],
  ...osc,
  [A(2059.91), 1.14, 'f#4', .27, { release: 2 }],          // the bloom's top F# (v4)
  [A(2062.8), 2.5, 'd4', .1, { release: 2.5 }],        // "forty": long (Cyc's 39 rings); its low D2 in the contrabass
  [A(2064.47), .3, 'a4', .14, { release: .5 }],          // "two": short
  [A(2066.49), .1, 'd5', .15, { release: .12 }],          // "one match, a day": the shortest tick
  [A(2067.67), 1.4, 'd4', .16, { release: 2 }],         // "The newest still burn": a held D, still lit (v5: gone before 'One lantern')
  [A(2082.71), .49, 'a3', .16, { release: 1.5 }], [A(2083.2), .6, 'd4', .16, { release: 1.6 }],   // the last slip, on the cut (v4); v5: the
  // celesta lets go almost at once and the strings take the held D (L1517's 250-2k band was 2.4 dB clear of the celesta's ring)
  [A(2105.46), .78, 'a3', .34, { release: 3 }], [A(2106.24), 3, 'd4', .38, { release: 7 }],       // the new candle ('b6' 2106.24)
], { release: 1.4 })
  .s('gm_celesta').room(.7).rsize(5).orbit(4)

// HARMONY: low strings + contrabass. D under "Learning"; the network's floor (soft); the bloom; then the slip's
// A-E fifth and the last chord's A-E beneath the held D (Asus4).
$: line([
  [A(2049.35), 5.8, '[d2,a2]', .04, { attack: .8 }],
  [A(2058.09), 1.15, '[d2,a2]', .14 * W3, { attack: .3, release: .5 }],
  [A(2085.25), 7.6, '[a1,e2]', .04, { attack: 2.5, release: 1.2 }],
  [A(2107.8), 2.5, '[a1,e2,a2,e3]', .167, { attack: 1.4, release: 6, lpf: 900 }],
], { attack: 1, release: 2, lpf: 700 })
  .s('gm_string_ensemble_1').hpf(40).room(.6).rsize(5).orbit(5)
$: line([
  [A(2049.35), 5.8, 'd2', .055, { attack: .8 }],
  [A(2058.09), 1.15, 'd2', .24 * W3, { attack: .2, release: .5 }],
  [A(2059.91), 1.14, 'd2', .27, { attack: .15, release: .35 }],   // the bloom's floor (v4)
  [A(2062.8), 3.2, 'd2', .08, { attack: .6, release: 1.5 }],   // "forty": the low, long D under the celesta
  [A(2085.25), 7.6, 'a1', .055, { attack: 2.5, release: 1.2 }],
  [A(2107.8), 2.5, 'a1', .24, { attack: 1.2, release: 5 }],
], { attack: 1, release: 2 })
  .s('gm_contrabass').hpf(50).lpf(400).room(.5).rsize(5).orbit(5)

// HIGH STRINGS (above the voice): LEARNING lit in D major; the network's top on "network" (a third); the held D
// of "still burn"; the dark lantern's single E; the slip's held D; the new candle's held D (the suspension).
$: line([
  [A(2049.35), 5.8, '[d5,f#5,a5]', .02, { attack: 1.2, lpf: 1800 }],   // v5: a halo, not a bed
  [A(2058.09), 1.15, '[a5,d6]', .1 * W3 * WH, { attack: .4, release: .5 }],
  [A(2067.67), 2.0, 'd5', .05, { attack: .8, release: 1 }],
  [A(2070.35), 7.35, 'e5', .065, { attack: 1.5, release: .6 }],    // v5: -3.7 dB under L1516/L1516b (250-2k margin was 4.5)
  [A(2077.7), 4.65, 'e5', .1, { attack: 1.2, release: 1.5 }],      // v5: re-bowed in the clear after 'That file stays open':
                                                                     // the question carries the hold to the cut (2082.71) at full v4 level   // v3: held to the cut (2082.71), the question unanswered
  [A(2083.2), 9.49, 'd5', .045, { attack: 1.8, release: 1.2 }],   // v4: from the slip's D (2083.2)
  [A(2106.24), 3.5, 'd5', .083, { attack: 1.2, release: 6 }],
], { attack: 1, release: 2, lpf: 2600 })
  .s('gm_string_ensemble_1').room(.7).rsize(6).orbit(6)

// ---- THE NETWORK: M3's forward wave, one era instrument per column, all at a third under the line;
// anything between D3 and D5 behind lpf 900 ----
const rip = (t, ns, v) => ns.map((n, i) => [A(t) + .11 * i, i === 3 ? .2 : .11, n, v * W3])
// valve organ (low, its top D3 filtered), then its held fifth
$: line([...rip(2055.9, ['d2', 'f#2', 'a2', 'd3'], .22), [A(2056.34), 2.9, '[d2,a2]', .15 * W3, { attack: .3, release: .5 }]], { release: .3 })
  .s('gm_drawbar_organ').lpf(700).room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(7)   // v5: lpf 900 -> 700 (its upper partials sat in 1-4 kHz)
// cello (low), then its held A
$: line([...rip(2056.34, ['a1', 'd2', 'f#2', 'a2'], .24), [A(2056.78), 2.45, 'a2', .16 * W3, { attack: .2, release: .5 }]], { release: .4 })
  .s('gm_cello').lpf(900).room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(7)
// piano (high), then soft high pings
$: line([...rip(2056.78, ['d5', 'f#5', 'a5', 'd6'], .2 * WH), [A(2057.32), .5, 'f#6', .12 * W3 * WH], [A(2057.82), .5, 'a6', .12 * W3 * WH], [A(2058.32), .5, 'f#6', .13 * W3 * WH], [A(2058.82), .4, 'a6', .13 * W3 * WH]], { release: 1 })
  .s('piano').room(.5).rsize(3).orbit(7)
// the GPU-era oscillator pulse (low eighths, its D3 filtered), stopping as the line ends
const pulse = []
for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) pulse.push([A(2057.22) + .22 * i, .2, ['d2', 'd3', 'a2', 'd3'][i % 4], .5])
$: line(pulse).s('sawtooth').lpf(900).attack(.005).decay(.18).sustain(0).release(.05).gain(.16 * W3).orbit(7)
// harp (high)
$: line([...rip(2057.66, ['d5', 'f#5', 'a5', 'd6'], .24 * WH), [A(2058.32), .5, 'a5', .14 * W3 * WH], [A(2058.82), .4, 'd6', .14 * W3 * WH]], { release: 1.5 })
  .s('gm_orchestral_harp').room(.5).rsize(3).orbit(7)
// pizz (low, its D3 filtered) on "network"
$: line([...rip(2058.09, ['d2', 'f#2', 'a2', 'd3'], .32), [A(2058.61), .3, 'd2', .26 * W3], [A(2059.01), .2, 'a1', .22 * W3]], { release: .4 })
  .s('gm_pizzicato_strings').lpf(900).room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(7)

// THE BLOOM (2059.35–2060.65, in the gap after "all along"; L1515 starts 2061.51): the trained forward pass lands
// on F#: full D major, the film's fullest moment, gone before the next line.
// v4 (critic round 1): the whole gap is used; the chord lands on F# (2059.91) and HOLDS at full D major to 2061.05,
// releasing so the texture is thin by 2061.35; about 4 dB louder than v3: the loudest moment of the score.
